<title>UK: CLM says could revise HCG offer.</title>
<headline>CLM says could revise HCG offer.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>CLM Insurance Fund Plc said it was in talks with the advisers of HCG Lloyd's Investment Trust Plc which may lead to a revision of its offer for HCG.</p>
<p>CLM urged shareholders of HCG to take no action for the moment and &quot;in particular not to accept the offer by the Benfield and Rea Investment Trust Plc (BRIT)&quot;.</p>
<p>The proposed CLM/HCG merger was thrown into turmoil when BRIT announced a hostile takeover offer for HCG on August 15.</p>
<p>BRIT's offer is thought to be worth around 78 million stg compared to CLM's original offer of 72 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
